    "body": "<!-- hive-mind:working-session-summary -->\n## Working session summary\n\nPlanned, not executed: https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3785.\n\nThe requested work remains unverified. The plan below describes intended steps; writing or reading a plan record does not verify delivery. Plan:\n\n````lino\ngeneral_change_plan\n  id \"repository_work_item_plan_e99fea20f20d8cab\"\n  execution_mode \"repository_work_item\"\n  terminal_state \"planned_not_executed\"\n  goal \"/limits display needs to be fixed\\n\\n<img width=\\\"722\\\" height=\\\"786\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/35db5ed9-b6cf-476e-b237-c745aa53d7d2\\\" />\\n\\n```\\nClaude limits\\nClaude authentication expired. Please use `/solve` or `/hive` commands to trigger re-authentication of Claude.\\n```\\n\\nIs not displayed in separate section as Codex is.\\n\\nWe also don't recognize the situation where `claude` subscription is not available at all, as it was cancelled, we need to double check if we can do so without auth. If not, missing auth display stays, but it must be in separate section as we do with Codex.\\n\\n```\\nChatGPT Pro subscription (ends in 10d 16h 36m; Nov 5, 7:22am UTC)\\nCodex authentication expired. Please re-authenticate Codex with your ChatGPT account.\\n```\\n\\nCodex shows strange situation, we have `codex (pending: 0, processing: 1)` meaning one codex tasks is succesfully executed, and yet for some reason we cannot get data about the subscription.\\n\\n<img width=\\\"1824\\\" height=\\\"1112\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2b1b5b92-b137-44ce-92c0-cea615c3abc7\\\" />\\n\\nThis is how it looks in `chatgpt.com`, and looks like recently it worked, but now it does not work.\\n\\nWe also need to double check if we can get information about when subscription expires for the Claude MAX, so next time we will have this subscription we will get exact timing and date, we should double check if there any way documented online in GitHub or other resources (not only official ones).\\n\\nMay be we see some clues here: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/konard/private-logs/main/home-box/310adb4926cd6c77/hive-telegram-bot.log.txt need to download all logs and data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data to `./docs/case-studies/issue-{id}` folder, and use it to do deep case study analysis (also make sure to search online for additional facts and data), in which we will reconstruct timeline/sequence of events, list of each and all requirements from the issue, find root causes of the each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement (we should also check known existing components/libraries, that solve similar problem or can help in solutions).\\n\\nIf there is not enough data to find actual root cause, add debug output and verbose mode if not present, that will allow us to find root cause on next iteration.\\n\\nIf issue related to any other repository/project, where we can report issues on GitHub, please do so. Each issue must contain reproducible examples, workarounds and suggestions for fix the issue in code. Also double check to fully apply requirements to entire codebase, so if we have issue in multiple places, it should be fixed in all them.\\n\\nPlease plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.\"\n  target \"https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3785\"\n  step 1\n    capability \"Fetch\"\n    action \"read the referenced work item at https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3785 before planning any change\"\n    expected_evidence \"the work-item text naming the artifact the change must produce\"\n  step 2\n    capability \"Write\"\n    action \"append the bounded repository work-item plan to .formal-ai/general-change-plan.lino\"\n    expected_evidence \"the exact repository work-item goal and execution boundary\"\n````\n\n> ⚠️ This pull request still contains no changes - nothing was implemented yet.\n\n---\n*This summary was automatically extracted from the AI working session output.*",
